The main logic is implemented in a method called loadTheArk, which takes a collection of candidate animals as input and returns the number of valid pairs formed. Inside this method, animals are sorted using a custom comparator that orders them first by species and then by gender. This ensures that animals of the same species and opposite genders are grouped together for pairing.

